From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: Save states from another build of the core load, with a warning

Azahar refuses a state whose header names another source revision, so every
core update orphans the states made with the one before. The test build of
1.3 shipped 2126.2; this core is 2126.1.2 with the azahar-nano changes, and
both serialize the same data: Super Mario 3D Land's RetroArch state from
2126.2 loads and plays on it. A mismatch is now a warning.

diff --git a/src/core/savestate.cpp b/src/core/savestate.cpp
index 2b98067..4cb4989 100644
--- a/src/core/savestate.cpp
+++ b/src/core/savestate.cpp
@@ -519,11 +519,13 @@ bool System::LoadStateBuffer(std::vector<u8> buffer) {
         return false;
     }
     std::string revision = fmt::format("{:02x}", fmt::join(header.revision, ""));
+    // dArkOS: a state from another build of the core still loads (with a warning), so a
+    // core update does not orphan every state. The states of 2126.2 and of 2126.1.2 with
+    // the azahar-nano changes serialize the same data.
     if (revision != Common::g_scm_rev) {
-        LOG_ERROR(Core,
-                  "Save state file created from a different revision (core: {}, savestate: {})",
-                  Common::g_scm_rev, revision);
-        return false;
+        LOG_WARNING(Core,
+                    "Save state file created from a different revision (core: {}, savestate: {})",
+                    Common::g_scm_rev, revision);
     }
 
     std::vector<u8> state(buffer.begin() + sizeof(CSTHeader), buffer.end());
